fseek(f, 0, SEEK_SET);            // rewind input file
*(uint*)(ctx + 0x22c) = 0;        // reset record/cursor index

uint width  = *(uint*)(ctx + 0x24c);                    // local_38
uint blocks = *(uint*)(ctx + 0x250) / *(uint*)(ctx + 0x270);  // uVar16
uint rows   = blocks / width;                           // local_3c
uint words  = width >> 2;                               // local_34 (width/4)

if (width <= blocks) { ... /* TRUNCATED */ }
```

The field relationships suggest: `0x270` = items per raw chunk, `0x250` = total item count, `0x24c` = items per record/group (with `0x34` = number of 32-bit words per record), `0x22c` = current record index being reset before a reload pass, and `0x1098` = the open input `FILE*`. The truncated remainder is a per-record loop (bounded by `width` vs. `blocks`) that almost certainly parses the file into the context's buffers.

