## Part 1 — What the function does

This is the classic **`dealwithargs` command-line parser from the Olden "voronoi" benchmark**, protected with control-flow flattening (the `local_94` variable is a dispatcher state; each `if`-chain arm is one basic block of the original program, and the `bVar2`/`iVar1` + `goto LAB_0010131e` pattern implements a conditional state transition).

Behavior:

- Takes `argc` (`param_1`) and `argv` (`param_2`).
- Reads up to three arguments: `size` (`argv[1]`, default 32), `procs` (`argv[2]`, default 1), `numnodes` (`argv[3]`, default 1), storing `numnodes` and `procs` into two globals (`DAT_00115070`, `DAT_00115078` — the huge additive constant is an obfuscated addressing artifact, not a real offset).
- If `procs > 1`, computes the hypercube dimension `dim` = smallest `d` with `2^d >= procs` (an unrolled `while (stride < procs) stride *= 2, dim++` loop) and stores it in a third global (`DAT_00115080`).
- Prints `"Voronoi with %d size on %d procs of dim %d\n"` and **returns `size`**.

## Part 2 — Reconstructed pseudocode

```c
/* Globals (deobfuscated names) */
int NumNodes;   /* DAT_00115070 - set from argv[3] */
int Procs;      /* DAT_00115078 - set from argv[2] */
int Dim;        /* DAT_00115080 - derived from Procs */

uint dealwithargs(int argc, char **argv)
{
    int  size, procs, dim, stride;

    /* --- numnodes: 4th argument, default 1 --- */
    if (argc > 3)
        NumNodes = atoi(argv[3]);       /* strtol(..., 10) */
    else
        NumNodes = 1;

    /* --- procs: 3rd argument, default 1 --- */
    if (argc >= 3)                      /* argc == 3 or argc > 3 both parse argv[2] */
        Procs = atoi(argv[2]);
    else
        Procs = 1;

    /* --- size: 2nd argument, default 32 --- */
    if (argc > 1)
        size = atoi(argv[1]);
    else {
        /* argc <= 1: pure-default path */
        Dim = 0;
        printf("Voronoi with %d size on %d procs of dim %d\n", 32, 1, 0);
        return 32;
    }

    /* --- dimension of the processor hypercube --- */
    procs = Procs;
    if (procs > 1) {
        dim = 0;
        for (stride = 1; stride < procs; stride *= 2)
            dim++;
        /* dim = ceil(log2(procs)) = smallest d with 2^d >= procs */
    } else {
        dim = 0;
    }
    Dim = dim;

    printf("Voronoi with %d size on %d procs of dim %d\n", size, Procs, dim);
    return (uint)size;
}
```

